timeline.body:
Code level changes LGTM!

One sanity check around behavior: before this PR, the audit log told us how many operations there were, albeit very inefficiently, by virtue of there being one `BulkItemRequest` entry per item. 

Now, that information is lost, e.g.,:

```
curl -k -u "elastic-admin:elastic-password" -X POST "http://localhost:9200/_bulk?refresh=true" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d'
{ "index" : { "_index" : "<index-2-{now/d}>", "_id" : "1" } }
{ "field1" : "value1" }
{ "index" : { "_index" : "<index-2-{now/d}>", "_id" : "2" } }
{ "field1" : "value2" }
```

Produces a single `BulkItemRequest` entry. I wonder if it makes sense to add a new field `item_count` or similar to indicate how many items there were.

Apologies if I missed something and this information is actually captured.

